WEBVTT

00:17.590 --> 00:19.700
Are they still not coming today?

00:19.700 --> 00:22.430
Mayumori–san and Miyazaki–san.

00:22.430 --> 00:23.220
Yeah.

00:23.770 --> 00:25.910
What if they never do?

00:26.590 --> 00:33.240
With the recital over, attending
practice over the break is optional.

00:33.240 --> 00:34.270
Yeah...

00:34.270 --> 00:36.090
It's a pretty strange feeling.

00:36.560 --> 00:41.010
Like, it took me until now to realize.

00:42.130 --> 00:45.040
Turns out I really enjoy being in the club.

00:51.350 --> 00:54.480
Was that the best you could do?
Was it really?

01:22.550 --> 01:24.160
Why are you still here?

01:25.450 --> 01:26.540
Don't you have your club?

01:29.450 --> 01:35.050
Try as you might to be careful,
but it could still easily fall apart.

01:35.650 --> 01:38.510
That's another thing that
makes it like a mille–feuille.

01:39.270 --> 01:40.460
Uta–chan...

01:42.220 --> 01:44.350
Morning, you two.

01:44.350 --> 01:46.860
Good morning.

01:48.940 --> 01:51.230
For today's practice...

01:51.530 --> 01:53.460
U–Um, President.

01:54.500 --> 01:57.710
I–I'd like to know.

01:57.710 --> 02:02.540
What happened during our performance,
and what upset Musubu–chan.

02:04.120 --> 02:08.590
I don't want things to end
with me still in the dark.

02:23.430 --> 02:29.220
"Harmony of Mille–Feuille"

03:39.160 --> 03:42.910
"Things That Change"

03:42.910 --> 03:46.540
My summer break starts now!

03:51.750 --> 03:54.630
They're probably practicing now.

04:00.740 --> 04:03.430
Well? Notice anything?

04:06.590 --> 04:08.120
Um...

04:08.570 --> 04:09.810
No need to be shy.

04:10.160 --> 04:15.680
It's not by much, but Musubu–chan
wasn't harmonizing with the chorus.

04:15.680 --> 04:17.860
At least it sounded that way, or maybe not.

04:18.250 --> 04:21.110
No, you're right. I thought so, too.

04:21.510 --> 04:23.970
Th–That's impossible, though.

04:23.970 --> 04:27.610
Musubu–chan has perfect pitch,
be it her hearing or singing.

04:27.880 --> 04:30.470
Have you noticed anything else?

04:30.930 --> 04:32.200
Um...

04:32.790 --> 04:34.370
I think Kuma–chan has.

04:36.830 --> 04:39.630
The rhythm sped up.

04:41.400 --> 04:42.390
Yup.

04:42.390 --> 04:44.400
By quite a bit.

04:44.400 --> 04:46.970
Correct. You've gotten better at this.

04:47.520 --> 04:52.060
Ururu–chan was never
this off–beat during practice.

04:52.950 --> 04:54.250
Was she nervous?

04:54.250 --> 04:56.430
She certainly didn't seem to be.

05:01.550 --> 05:03.310
Was it the clapping?

05:03.820 --> 05:09.570
Yes. Ururu–chan gradually sped up her vocal
percussion to match the audience's claps.

05:12.280 --> 05:14.150
She's still a beginner, after all.

05:14.620 --> 05:17.530
Her rhythm was thrown off
by the audience's beat.

05:17.820 --> 05:20.110
I never noticed...

05:20.110 --> 05:21.430
Me neither...

05:22.260 --> 05:24.490
I doubt Ururu–chan herself noticed.

05:25.140 --> 05:29.250
That's all part of performing
on stage for the first time.

05:29.610 --> 05:33.150
Without noticing the quickening rhythm,

05:33.150 --> 05:37.210
Uta–chan and Kuma–chan became
unable to maintain the right pitch.

05:41.240 --> 05:44.460
We sang at a slightly higher note?

05:44.460 --> 05:45.100
That's right.

05:46.420 --> 05:50.580
Kuma–chan's bass went up
a tiny bit from here onwards.

05:50.580 --> 05:51.820
It did...

05:51.820 --> 05:56.060
As a result, Uta–chan's lead vocals
also became higher pitched.

05:56.060 --> 05:57.660
S–Sorry about that.

05:57.660 --> 05:59.690
Me too... I'm sorry.

06:00.500 --> 06:02.360
Nah, don't be.

06:02.360 --> 06:06.600
It's natural that Ururu–chan
became lost in the excitement.

06:06.600 --> 06:08.740
I–Is it?

06:09.280 --> 06:11.780
That happens all the time in a cappella.

06:11.780 --> 06:15.900
If anything, that's where
the true appeal of a cappella lies.

06:17.780 --> 06:20.160
How do I put it? Give me a sec.

06:26.370 --> 06:27.870
Uta–chan, Kuma–chan.

06:27.870 --> 06:30.510
How many pitches are there
on a musical scale?

06:30.840 --> 06:34.210
Err, C, C–sharp, D...

06:34.210 --> 06:35.720
Is it 12?

06:36.000 --> 06:37.680
Yup, you got it.

06:38.170 --> 06:44.140
To put it simply, we're dividing
sound into 12 parts.

06:44.690 --> 06:50.580
So an A note that falls short of
an A–sharp is just a slightly higher A,

06:50.580 --> 06:54.400
while not hitting A–flat
means a slightly lower A.

06:57.050 --> 06:58.870
I can tell that I lost you.

06:59.150 --> 07:03.720
The frequency of an A is typically 440 Hz.

07:03.720 --> 07:08.750
Meanwhile, an A–sharp is 466.164 Hz.

07:09.100 --> 07:11.490
We generally can't hear it,

07:11.490 --> 07:16.700
but the fact remains that there's
a difference between 440 Hz and 441 Hz.

07:18.620 --> 07:20.980
I think we need a different explanation.

07:20.980 --> 07:24.210
Unlike instruments,
humans can't be precisely tuned,

07:24.210 --> 07:25.680
plus we're affected by our mood.

07:26.240 --> 07:28.350
You may think you hit an A note,

07:28.350 --> 07:31.140
yet it isn't necessarily a perfect A.

07:31.730 --> 07:33.900
Oh, I know that one!

07:33.900 --> 07:36.410
Like when I should have gotten it
right during the tuning,

07:36.410 --> 07:38.400
but it doesn't actually feel like I did.

07:38.400 --> 07:42.900
That's right, our ears can more or less tell.

07:42.900 --> 07:47.620
It's actually quite hard to be
on pitch in the truest sense.

07:48.500 --> 07:49.450
Yeah...

07:49.720 --> 07:52.760
Isn't a cappella difficult to begin with?

07:52.760 --> 07:55.420
You're forced to hear
other people's sounds and all.

07:55.420 --> 07:59.580
Yeah, I was pretty bad at first
because the chorus distracted me.

08:00.150 --> 08:04.210
Uh–huh, and you have to sing
your part correctly despite that.

08:05.720 --> 08:08.490
That applies to everyone, doesn't it?

08:08.490 --> 08:12.580
Yup. You have to maintain a rhythm
while matching the others.

08:13.180 --> 08:14.470
Th–That's just...

08:15.220 --> 08:16.740
Impossible, right?

08:16.740 --> 08:18.010
Eh...

08:18.010 --> 08:20.320
Because it is. We're not machines.

08:20.700 --> 08:23.980
That's my view of a cappella.

08:24.540 --> 08:27.680
You adjust your performance
through eye contact.

08:27.680 --> 08:31.110
Go with what feels fun,
coordination be damned.

08:31.530 --> 08:36.070
Better yet, turn that chaotic rhythm
into something to groove to.

08:36.070 --> 08:38.270
Giving a one of a kind performance,

08:38.270 --> 08:41.730
wholly unique to the members
coming together then and there

08:41.730 --> 08:44.120
is what it's all about, if you ask me.

08:44.120 --> 08:47.580
I personally consider
our last show a success.

08:47.580 --> 08:50.860
So, are you saying
you noticed that we were off,

08:50.860 --> 08:55.450
and opted to match
your performance with ours?

08:55.450 --> 08:56.800
Pretty much.

08:56.800 --> 09:00.510
If one of us is out of tune,
then we may as well all be.

09:01.240 --> 09:06.940
It may not be correct, but that
doesn't mean we can't harmonize.

09:06.940 --> 09:10.100
Except Mayumori–san refused to compromise.

09:10.100 --> 09:14.460
Yeah, Musubu–chan has perfect pitch.

09:14.460 --> 09:18.060
Perfect enough to notice
that 1 Hz difference.

09:18.680 --> 09:20.360
The way I see it,

09:20.360 --> 09:25.980
Musubu–chan operates on a more
detailed musical scale than the 12 we use.

09:26.670 --> 09:30.360
Her delicate ear for music is
why even being a semitone off

09:30.360 --> 09:34.470
must sound grating to her,
even though it means nothing to us.

09:40.520 --> 09:45.070
People with perfect pitch
tend to not be fans of a cappella.

09:46.670 --> 09:53.640
I think Musubu–chan finds it hard to accept
singing incorrectly as a valid approach.

09:54.170 --> 09:55.770
Does that mean...

09:55.770 --> 09:59.200
In a way, we were the ones in the wrong.

10:00.420 --> 10:05.680
During the recital, Musubu–chan was
the only one who stuck to the score.

10:07.660 --> 10:08.940
Cut the crap!

10:10.460 --> 10:12.320
Oh, I get it...

10:12.680 --> 10:15.130
Instead of one person following the score,

10:15.130 --> 10:18.570
a cappella works better with everyone
on the same page, even if the wrong one.

10:19.330 --> 10:23.660
That said, a cappella bands who align
with Musubu–chan's beliefs do exist.

10:24.430 --> 10:27.730
She's not wrong for wanting
everything to be precise.

10:27.730 --> 10:31.770
After all, pulling it off leads
to an even greater harmony.

10:42.800 --> 10:45.260
"For Beginners! Basic Beatboxing Tips"

10:45.850 --> 10:48.350
There's no one true answer to this.

10:51.630 --> 10:53.590
Not when neither side is wrong.

10:54.190 --> 10:56.150
"A Cappella Club (First–years)
Uta sent a sticker"

10:59.030 --> 11:01.980
Uta–chan... What would you like to do?

11:24.080 --> 11:26.600
We met up! Thank god.

11:26.600 --> 11:29.410
Right? What happened to your yukata?

11:29.410 --> 11:31.260
I considered it.

11:31.260 --> 11:35.470
It's just that our classmates
might be at the festival.

11:35.820 --> 11:39.320
I thought they'll think I'm the type
who keeps a low profile in class,

11:39.320 --> 11:42.800
while partying hard
at festivals and the like.

11:43.330 --> 11:44.600
How about you?

11:44.600 --> 11:48.390
I figured you'd think along those lines.

11:49.260 --> 11:54.860
If people saw only me wearing a yukata,
they might think we don't get along.

11:56.420 --> 11:57.820
Where to now?

11:57.820 --> 12:00.240
The festival, where else?

12:00.240 --> 12:03.540
I haven't been to a festival
with friends since elementary.

12:04.690 --> 12:07.660
I only go to festivals with my family.

12:07.980 --> 12:10.980
Where do we even start with festivals?

12:11.440 --> 12:12.530
Good question...

12:12.530 --> 12:15.170
What even is the purpose
of attending a festival?

12:15.170 --> 12:19.810
Never thought of it...
Wanna grab a bite from a stall?

12:19.810 --> 12:20.980
Oh, sure!

12:21.890 --> 12:24.090
Wait, I had fried rice before coming.

12:24.680 --> 12:26.490
Oh, you did...

12:26.490 --> 12:27.670
Cooked with mustard greens.

12:28.090 --> 12:29.360
Must've been yummy.

12:30.600 --> 12:31.660
Wanna walk around?

12:31.660 --> 12:33.420
Yeah, let's do that.

12:46.790 --> 12:48.700
I knew you'd be here.

12:49.430 --> 12:51.200
How did you know?

12:52.310 --> 12:55.930
Doesn't that line make me sound
like a master manipulator?

12:55.930 --> 12:58.960
I didn't know you enjoyed
theatrics, President.

12:58.960 --> 13:02.000
Oh, so you still think of me
as your president!

13:04.810 --> 13:06.750
You have a mean streak, you know that?

13:08.190 --> 13:09.840
Aren't you going to the festival?

13:10.430 --> 13:11.720
I already did.

13:12.900 --> 13:13.720
Want some?

13:14.760 --> 13:17.180
Sure do! Can I?

13:18.140 --> 13:20.560
Here. I bought extra.

13:20.560 --> 13:22.220
Thanks for the food.

13:29.230 --> 13:30.900
Aren't you gonna ask me?

13:31.650 --> 13:32.660
Ask what?

13:33.060 --> 13:37.700
About the recital, and how
I stopped going to practice.

13:37.700 --> 13:39.800
That did happen, yes.

13:39.800 --> 13:41.630
There you go playing dumb.

13:41.630 --> 13:45.100
I hate how you refuse to speak your mind.

13:45.100 --> 13:46.330
I know.

13:47.170 --> 13:54.290
I remember when you said that
being perfect is no good in a cappella.

13:55.580 --> 13:58.700
Our last performance was
what you were getting at.

14:00.020 --> 14:03.930
Look, I get it. I'm not dumb.

14:03.930 --> 14:05.140
I see.

14:05.830 --> 14:08.240
Even so, I...

14:26.600 --> 14:28.970
This sure is a fun festival.

14:28.970 --> 14:29.920
Yeah...

14:29.920 --> 14:31.770
I have you to thank for it.

14:31.770 --> 14:34.490
If anything, I'm grateful to you.

14:38.990 --> 14:44.080
I wish Miyazaki–san and
Mayumori–san had joined us.

14:44.080 --> 14:46.140
I feel the same way.

14:48.970 --> 14:52.570
Kuma–chan, please hear me out.

14:52.570 --> 14:54.470
Sure, go ahead.

14:54.890 --> 15:00.200
I don't want things with Musubu–chan
and Ururu–chan to say this way.

15:01.180 --> 15:05.240
I probably shouldn't assume
that I understand her...

15:05.240 --> 15:09.130
Still, it must be hard on Musubu–chan.

15:09.130 --> 15:11.690
Considering her goals
aren't in line with ours.

15:15.070 --> 15:17.700
We've been there before.

15:18.340 --> 15:25.160
Like being grouped with people who are
friends and not getting their inside jokes.

15:25.670 --> 15:26.500
Yeah...

15:26.940 --> 15:29.120
You feel alone and alienated...

15:31.420 --> 15:39.270
Plus, well... Unlike a weakling like me,
Musubu–chan has a strong will.

15:42.620 --> 15:43.810
Amazing!

15:43.810 --> 15:45.180
That was cool!

15:45.890 --> 15:51.030
She must've hated being applauded
for something she felt was terrible.

15:51.030 --> 15:55.560
It's as though she's being told that
aiming for greater heights is pointless.

15:55.920 --> 15:58.690
We should be trying to make good music!

15:58.690 --> 16:00.020
So what if we're a club?!

16:00.020 --> 16:02.580
She must've been so frustrated.

16:02.580 --> 16:07.990
What she believes to be the right
approach isn't shared by anyone else.

16:08.610 --> 16:11.020
Maybe I'm getting ahead of myself here,

16:11.020 --> 16:14.240
but I think she's been
enjoying our club activities.

16:14.700 --> 16:19.670
Yet music means so much more
to her than the club itself.

16:26.380 --> 16:32.120
A–As for me, I enjoy singing,
and I also enjoy a cappella!

16:52.830 --> 16:56.860
I haven't made head or tails
of what the president said.

16:56.860 --> 17:01.320
I don't have an answer yet, and I may never.

17:01.780 --> 17:06.380
We live in separate worlds,
our sights set on different things.

17:06.380 --> 17:09.750
Now might be the only time
we'll spend together.

17:10.080 --> 17:15.690
That's why I don't want a cappella to
become a bitter memory to Musubu–chan.

17:17.160 --> 17:20.720
We have to avoid that.
I want to think of a way.

17:22.260 --> 17:23.550
You're so right.

17:24.740 --> 17:29.350
I feel the same way. I want to do something.

17:29.850 --> 17:32.590
Let's make it happen... together.

17:33.150 --> 17:33.980
Yeah.

17:45.850 --> 17:48.260
I knew this would happen.

17:50.330 --> 17:52.630
Why aren't you here, Reirei?

17:59.410 --> 18:02.540
Mom, I need a towel...

18:03.120 --> 18:04.790
Uta! Welcome back!

18:05.790 --> 18:07.550
Sis?! Why are you here?

18:08.590 --> 18:10.340
Why are you all wet?

18:20.820 --> 18:23.350
Time goes by so slowly...

18:26.810 --> 18:30.790
Was summer break always like this?

18:32.860 --> 18:35.780
"Kuma: This is the video
of our recital. Please watch."

18:37.100 --> 18:38.830
What for?

18:39.740 --> 18:41.300
"Uh, no? Why would I? I'm traumatized here"

18:41.300 --> 18:43.700
"Kuma: Please, you really should.
I want to hear your thoughts"

18:46.920 --> 18:49.120
Not like I have anything better to do.

18:50.060 --> 18:52.860
Hello, we're the a cappella club.

18:54.170 --> 18:58.510
We're a small club
that only took off this year.

18:58.510 --> 19:00.630
I hope you'll show us your support.

19:01.520 --> 19:05.470
A cappella is performing music
entirely with vocals.

19:09.310 --> 19:11.560
Uta's such a funny girl.

19:18.110 --> 19:19.870
Looks like a good time...

19:23.170 --> 19:25.250
Hey, this rocks...

19:25.250 --> 19:28.320
I have no idea what Omusubi
was going on about.

19:33.740 --> 19:35.700
"Uta: Do you think Ururu–chan will be fine?"

19:40.590 --> 19:42.050
Ready, and...

19:42.050 --> 19:44.590
Thank you very much!

19:54.170 --> 19:55.720
Wait a sec.

19:59.020 --> 20:02.140
Hold up. You're kidding me...

20:06.230 --> 20:08.060
What the heck is this?

20:09.900 --> 20:14.280
This is... I totally suck here...

20:14.560 --> 20:18.580
Hah, so you never noticed that
you're the one throwing everyone off?!

20:18.580 --> 20:20.370
How do you live with yourself?!

20:21.990 --> 20:25.610
It was my fault... all of it...

20:26.350 --> 20:28.240
That was a total mess...

20:29.070 --> 20:31.530
What the hell was I doing?

20:37.840 --> 20:39.800
"Ururu: Wish I didn't watch that"

20:42.260 --> 20:43.720
"Kuma – Audio call"

20:46.620 --> 20:47.980
What?

20:47.980 --> 20:50.110
Can we meet up?

21:03.380 --> 21:04.540
Miyazaki–san!

21:04.540 --> 21:05.230
Huh?

21:12.160 --> 21:14.240
K–Kuma–chan?

21:16.940 --> 21:19.160
Please come back to the club.

21:19.160 --> 21:21.250
What brought this on?

21:21.630 --> 21:26.460
I'm sure you don't want to quit
a cappella on sour terms.

21:27.110 --> 21:32.680
Says who? I've been
enjoying my nice, chill break.

21:32.680 --> 21:33.840
That's not true!

21:34.120 --> 21:35.130
Excuse me?

21:35.770 --> 21:37.670
That's not true!

21:37.670 --> 21:39.600
What makes you say that?

21:40.680 --> 21:45.090
I keep finding myself humming
the bass out of nowhere,

21:45.090 --> 21:49.770
and thinking about how to better
compliment your percussion.

21:52.690 --> 21:58.740
Thoughts about how our performance
could have been better cross my mind.

21:58.740 --> 22:02.540
I feel like my half–hearted
approach made it bad.

22:03.060 --> 22:05.710
I wish I had done more.

22:07.470 --> 22:11.830
It's vexing that this happened
when I tried to change myself...

22:13.480 --> 22:16.090
I'm sure you feel the same.

22:16.090 --> 22:19.340
Why are you acting like you know me?

22:19.340 --> 22:21.130
We're clubmates, nothing more.

22:22.150 --> 22:25.640
That's because we walk to school
every day over the break.

22:26.900 --> 22:28.540
That's it?

22:28.540 --> 22:29.340
Yeah.

22:29.340 --> 22:32.860
Our talks barely took off.
We were all awkward.

22:32.860 --> 22:34.850
That's true...

22:35.400 --> 22:38.140
It's not like that did us any good.

22:38.710 --> 22:40.570
Our performance still flopped...

22:41.160 --> 22:45.000
Yes. But, we spent time together.

22:45.550 --> 22:48.780
I got to pay attention to you.

22:51.170 --> 22:52.810
That's why I can tell.

22:55.540 --> 22:56.650
Let's turn this around.

22:57.660 --> 23:00.910
We can't let things end this way.

23:04.900 --> 23:06.500
Have you made up your mind?

23:06.910 --> 23:07.710
Rei?

23:08.140 --> 23:12.010
I can't say for sure.
Certainly not now, at least.

23:12.350 --> 23:13.010
Why not?

23:13.280 --> 23:17.170
All I want is to be with Airi.

23:17.170 --> 23:20.350
I only perform music
because I can do it with Airi.

23:20.730 --> 23:23.010
I like that! Nice friendship!

23:23.010 --> 23:23.870
Wrong.

23:23.870 --> 23:25.060
Really?

23:25.750 --> 23:28.150
They're unhealthily
dependent on each other.

23:28.440 --> 23:29.120
What?

23:30.290 --> 23:34.920
Come with me, Rei.
I'll set you on a more fitting path.
